  body: "# Evidence of care hours for CA\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe source directs acceptance of the claimant’s
    statement about the required care hours unless there is good reason to doubt it, and gives competing claims
    as an example requiring further enquiry.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe paragraph does not remove all conditions
    or make every statement conclusive. It does not authorise the project to collect care logs or claimant information.
    Where several people care for one person, the source has a separate election and decision process.\n\n## Inspected
    passages\n\n- [DMG 60040, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0fdcbb5e95ca5017ed9da/dmg-Chap-60.pdf#page=6).\n\
    - [DMG 60026, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0fdcbb5e95ca5017ed9da/dmg-Chap-60.pdf#page=4).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol10-ch60`:
    PDF `ab9fed933c167b4ac18039204c3853c425731ffb4239022a11b41884caaee22a`; extracted pages `bc5925c0d434fbc4bec575bea2e1e2dbd020b014497ab156973054e80e326f2f`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.596227Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0fdcbb5e95ca5017ed9da/dmg-Chap-60.pdf#page=6
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/ca-caring-condition
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The evidence instruction is specifically about the required hours of care.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch60/0006
      quote: "60040 The claimant’s statement that the required number of hours are spent in caring should be\naccepted
        without further enquiry unless there is good reason to doubt it.\n\n\nExample\n\n\nDenise and Lesley both
        claim CA for caring for Mick who is a severely disabled person. The DM decides\nto make further enquiries
        to establish who is entitled to CA (see DMG 60026)."
      locator: DMG 60040
